<title>INDIA: Indian base metals steady in dull trade.</title>
<headline>Indian base metals steady in dull trade.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Base metals were steady in dull trade on Wednesday, the Chrstmas day, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody is in a holiday mood,&quot; said a dealer.</p>
<p>Ready copper was quiet at 12,300 per quintal. Tin was steady at 34,300 rupees per quintal. Nickel was offered at 36,500 rupees per quintal. Aluminum was quoted at 7,250 rupees, zinc at 6,450 rupees and lead at 4,450 rupees per quintal.</p>
<p>--Bombay Commoditiies +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
